# BuildKit reads this for backend/Dockerfile, whose context is the repo root
# (a .dockerignore there would be root tooling). Only backend/, scout/ and
# scraper/ go in.
# It speeds up a local `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile` only: `wrangler
# deploy` passes the Dockerfile on stdin, so BuildKit skips this file and the
# Dockerfile's named COPYs are what keep .venv and vendor/ out.
*
!backend
!scout
!scraper
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/.env*
backend/vendor
backend/tests
backend/cloudflare
backend/.vercel
scout/tests
scraper/tests
